{"id":"l298n_line_follower","name":"L298N Line Follower","description":"Build a basic line-following robot: read the 3-channel line follower sensor (L, M, R) and steer two DC motors through the L298N, Motor A as the left wheel and Motor B as the right wheel. When the middle sensor detects the line, drive both motors forward. When only the left sensor detects the line, turn right by slowing or stopping the right motor; when only the right sensor detects the line, turn left the same way. When no sensor detects the line, stop both motors. Adjust the sensor threshold so a dark, weakly reflecting line reads raw HIGH (1), and reflective background reads raw LOW (0). Print the three raw sensor readings (0 or 1) and the action to the serial console once per control cycle; the action token is forward, left, right, or stop.","level":3,"parts":["l298n","line-sensor"],"targets":["atmega328p_arduino","atmega2560_arduino"],"application":"Presence and Distance","interface":"GPIO Input","protocols":["GPIO Input","GPIO/PWM Output"],"variants":{"atmega328p_arduino":{"circuit":{"boards":[{"id":"arduino-uno","boardKind":"arduino-uno","x":100,"y":100}],"components":[{"id":"DRIVER","metadataId":"l298n","x":550,"y":80,"properties":{"enaJumper":false,"enbJumper":false,"regulatorJumper":true,"sampleWindowMs":1000}},{"id":"BATTERY","metadataId":"battery-9v","x":550,"y":310},{"id":"SENSOR","metadataId":"line-sensor","x":780,"y":80,"properties":{"thresholdPosition":0.5,"leftPhotocurrentUa":300,"middlePhotocurrentUa":200,"rightPhotocurrentUa":300}}],"wires":[{"id":"w0","start":{"componentId":"arduino-uno","pinName":"5","x":0,"y":0},"end":{"componentId":"DRIVER","pinName":"IN1","x":0,"y":0},"color":"#4499cc","waypoints":[]},{"id":"w1","start":{"componentId":"arduino-uno","pinName":"6","x":0,"y":0},"end":{"componentId":"DRIVER","pinName":"IN2","x":0,"y":0},"color":"#4499cc","waypoints":[]},{"id":"w2","start":{"componentId":"arduino-uno","pinName":"11","x":0,"y":0},"end":{"componentId":"DRIVER","p